      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court dismissed the complaint for failure to state a claim, but the Ninth Circuit reversed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2017, Abdulkadir Masharipov carried out a terrorist attack on the Reina nightclub in Istanbul, Turkey, on behalf of the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria (ISIS), a designated Foreign Terrorist Organization."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Deputy Solicitor General Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Deputy Solicitor General Kneedler argued the cause for the United States as amicus curiae urging reversal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "plaintiffs sued three major social-media companies\u2014Face-\nbook, Inc., Google, Inc., and Twitter, Inc.\u2014claiming that they\naided and abetted ISIS and thus were liable for the Reina\nnightclub attack."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The parties here do not dispute that the frst three compo-\nnents of \u00a7 2333(d)(2) have been adequately alleged: The Reina\nnightclub attack was an \u201cact of international terrorism\u201d; the\nattack was \u201ccommitted, planned, or authorized\u201d by ISIS; and\nISIS was \u201cdesignated as a foreign terrorist organization\u201d as of the\ndate of the Reina nightclub attack. \u00a7 2333(d)(2)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Plaintiffs assert that it is \u201cthe person,\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Defendants",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "defendants insist that it is the \u201cact of international terrorism.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0002-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "To summarize the requirements of \u00a7 2333(d)(2), the phrase \u201caids and abets, by knowingly providing substantial assistance,\u201d points to the elements and factors articulated by Halberstam."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Defendants",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The mere creation of those platforms, however, is not culpable. To be sure, it might be that bad actors like ISIS are able to use platforms like defendants' for illegal\u2014and sometimes terrible\u2014ends. But the same could be said of cell phones, email, or the internet generally. Yet, we generally do not think that internet or cell service providers incur culpability merely for providing their services to the public writ large."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Plaintiffs have not made that showing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1496",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "cdc4dd9267003bf8e776f7557a8afa5d9050f30f6326821aa37709120a62cb19",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cdc4dd926700-0003-0004",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I join the opinion of the Court with the understanding that today's decisions are narrow in important respects."
    }
  ],
